gc8613 — the GC8613 sensor driver of the YIZHAN 4K camera (SigmaStar SSC8836 / Mercury6), in place of its stock
gc8613_MIPI.ko

Licence: MIT No Attribution (../../LICENSE) or, at your choice, the GNU General Public License version 2 (../COPYING).

Ours (OpenMicroCam): gc8613.c, mhal_sensor.h, modes.py and Kbuild, written for this project from the sensor's datasheet
and register semantics and mhal's sensor-driver interface (docs/firmware/components/mhal-csi-snr.md and
sensor-gc8613.md). The gain and the mirror / flip register procedures are the sensor maker's, as the public drivers for
this sensor write them.

The register values in tables/ are facts about the sensor, in our own form, each file with its origin:
- tables/stock.txt: as the camera's stock sensor driver programs the sensor, read from that module of the camera's flash;
  no text of its maker is carried.
- tables/rockchip.txt: the sensor maker's 40 fps setting as drivers/media/i2c/gc8613.c of Rockchip's Linux kernel carries
  it, in the maker's order (the same order stands in another vendor's driver of that setting family); the values only,
  none of that file's text.
- tables/shenshu.txt: from Shenshu's hi3516cv610 SDK sensor configuration, Copyright (c) 2001-2024 Shenshu Tech. Co., Ltd.;
  that file states no licence. Only the values are taken, as facts about the sensor, none of the file's text.
modes.py builds every mode's table from these and our changes to them; its output, modes.h, is made at build time.
